{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046635-arcana-dots-as-a-spell-factor","id":1046635,"title":"Arcana Dots as a Spell Factor","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-09T22:20:31-08:00","id":1046635,"title":"Arcana Dots as a Spell Factor","content":"Effects relying on dots in Fate were stripped away in the errata, and references to them were replaced with Potency, leaving the only spell factors used in the Arcanum as...spell factors. Appropriate.<br /> <br /> While playing my new Mage, I see that the same wasn't done for Forces - there are numerous effects that still use the Mage's Forces dots in some way. We've houseruled these over to Potency, but it does raise the question: Is it ever actually appropriate to use dot rating as a 'spell factor' (eg in Creative Thaumaturgy)? Even if the spell doesn't otherwise use Potency? It seems like a cheesy way to get free, but limited, power.<br /> <br /> Doing this in a Duration primary spell effectively grants the spell both Potency and Duration primary, since your primary factor always = your dots in the Arcanum anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T23:05:13-08:00","id":1046648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046635-arcana-dots-as-a-spell-factor#post1046635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While playing my new Mage, I see that the same wasn't done for Forces - there are numerous effects that still use the Mage's Forces dots in some way.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two, both of which serve more as a cap than a boost to the spell's abilities.<br /> <br /> Kinetic Efficiency specifically operates on the assumption that its primary benefits are not superlative, which makes allowing them to scale with a fully variable factor like Potency a poor fit \u2014 the spell is making its subject move more easily, not actually increasing the speed at which they move, which is why the Potency-based effect adds to fatigue rolls.<br /> <br /> The Reach effect for Zoom In doesn't override the basic effects of Potency in that spell and mapping the Reach benefit to Potency results in overt geometric expansion in a way that Fate boons giving you [Potency] uses of a +[Potency] bonus doesn't. (It's also modifying something that can make the difference between Sensory Range and more costly targeting mechanisms, which you necessarily want limited for a one-Reach effect on a two-dot spell that can already open up entire new targets.)<br /> <br /> If you care to apply the principle to Creative Thaum, I'd stick to using it for effects that you don't want to scale beyond five dots/levels/dice/etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}